{"name":"Three Ring Circus","hex":"#fddbb6","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"three ring circus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of three-ring circus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/three_ring_circus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Circus","blocks":[{"text":"A circus is a company of performers who put on diverse entertainment shows that may include clowns, acrobats, trained animals, trapeze acts, musicians, dancers, hoopers, tightrope walkers, jugglers, magicians, ventriloquists, and unicyclists as well as other object manipulation and stunt-oriented artists. The term \"circus\" also describes the field of performance, training, and community which has followed various formats through its 250-year modern history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg/330px-Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circus","wikidata":"Q47928"},{"title":"3 Ring Circus","blocks":[{"text":"3 Ring Circus is a 1954 American comedy film directed by Joseph Pevney and starring Dean Martin and Jerry Lewis. The picture was shot from February 17 to March 31, 1954, and was released at Christmas by Paramount Pictures. The supporting cast includes Joanne Dru, Zsa Zsa Gabor, Wallace Ford, Sig Ruman, Nick Cravat and Elsa Lanchester."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/23/3ringcircus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3_Ring_Circus","wikidata":"Q673099"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg/500px-Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Barnum_%26_Bailey_